'''Metalls del Yalabirga, S.A.''' ({{lang|ca|Metalls del Yalabirga}}) is a Balboan non-ferrous metals smelting and refining company operating in the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] foothills of [[Jala Province|Jala]]. Founded in 1979 as the second component of the BPP government's domestic processing chain for metals, the company smelts aluminium and refines copper and other non-ferrous metals from Yalabirga mining operations, using hydroelectric power from the Yalabirga river dams. The company is the primary domestic supplier of refined copper to Balboa's construction and manufacturing sectors.

The company is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker MYL. The [[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] holds a 6 per cent stake and the [[Balboa Pension Fund]] holds a 4 per cent stake.

